{"id": "idaho-2", "headline": "First CWD case found in Idaho Unit 13", "source": "Idaho Capital Sun", "url": "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/11/23/mule-deer-buck-tests-positive-for-cwd-in-idaho-near-oregon-border/", "published": "2026-11-23", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Idaho Fish and Game says a mule deer buck killed by a hunter along the Snake River, about half a mile from the Oregon border, tested positive for chronic wasting disease. It is the first detection in Unit 13 in Idaho County and the first outside units that previously had positive elk or deer. CWD is a contagious, incurable and fatal neurological disease that spreads among deer, elk and moose. It was first found in Idaho in 2021. Officials have tested more than 3,500 animals this year and ask the public to report road-killed or unusual deer and elk to support surveillance. Source: Idaho Capital Sun."], "qr": {"n": 37, "rows": ["1111111000011100111101110100001111111", "1000001010101111100011101111001000001", "1011101001111001100011111010101011101", "1011101011000110010000101101101011101", "1011101001010000001111010010001011101", "1000001011000011110000000001001000001", "1111111010101010101010101010101111111", "0000000001000010101111100010000000000", "1111101111001110010010111101110101010", "0111100111010000111110011010000101110", "0000011111001001010010001001001001101", "1101110001100011000001111011011101010", "1001101100001110010100000101111111101", "0011100110110010100110010100000100110", "1110111010001101111001100111010100111", "0010110001111001001011100010001011001", "0001001011000101011010101101111011101", "0000100011110100111111110010010100110", "1000111101100011000011100101101000111", "1111010100110011100001000000110000001", "1100111111011111010100101100011111111", "1001010110110100101111010010010101110", "0111111111001111111011101101111100011", "0011100001111011000101100011111000001", "1011001111001110010010101100011011111", "1010100000110010100111110100100100010", "100110101000010111001